senses.gloss:
वशि, इस्, m. subjugation, fascination, bewitching,
holding others in magical submission to the will;
(इ), n. the state of being subject, subjection.

वष्क् वष्क्, cl. 1. A., 10. P. वष्कते,
वष्कयति, &c., to see [cf. rt. विष्क्];
to go.

वाष्कल वाष्कल, अस्, आ, अम्, large, great;
(अस्), m. a warrior; a proper N.; (आस्), m. pl., N.
of a family or race (the descendants of Viśvā-mitra;
also written वास्कल).
